  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively provide relevant ingredients: rapid cooling can kinetically retain metastable phases in an as-cast HEA (R13), solidification can produce Laves phases or compositionally segregated dual-phase structures (R17, R20), and an antiferromagnetic constituent can reduce the magnetization of Fe/Co/Ni-based HEAs (R8). Several records also show that phase boundaries can pin defects or strengthen dual-phase materials. However, none identifies FeCoNiTi, an fcc/C14 combination in that system, Ti-sublattice antiferromagnetic coupling, C14-assisted magnetic domain-wall pinning, the distinct magnetic transitions, or the matched C14-dominant comparison composition. Thus the literature points broadly toward quench-controlled multiphase magnetic HEAs, but reconstructing the specific intervention and coercivity mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
